\title{Latest Deep-Dive}
\author{dhsorens}
\date{2026-08-20}
\meta{toc}{true}

\p{
    See my latest on [Fiat–Shamir and the random oracle model](dhsorens-002G) — the step that makes
    a proof system deployable, and the one whose security argument sits furthest from the deployed
    object. Khovratovich, Rothblum, and Soukhanov [proved false statements](dhsorens-0057) against
    Fiat–Shamir applied to a standard GKR-based argument, for every choice of hash function, so the
    qualifier that saves everything else is [adaptivity](dhsorens-004O), and it has to be checked
    system by system rather than assumed. It is the second written-out section of the [zkVMs and
    SNARKs](dhsorens-002C) corpus.
}
